WEBVTT

00:45.920 --> 00:49.132
That cake is so beautiful. It's so pretty.

00:49.716 --> 00:52.218
- Looks like someone's about to propose.
- I know!

00:55.180 --> 00:56.181
Ah…

01:04.939 --> 01:06.566
Hey.

01:06.649 --> 01:09.110
Hey, man. Not there.

01:09.194 --> 01:10.278
- Not here?
- No!

01:10.361 --> 01:11.362
Those two.

01:13.782 --> 01:16.034
Oh! Apologies.

01:20.538 --> 01:21.956
Sorry.

01:22.874 --> 01:25.001
- It's not them.
- Wow. How beautiful.

01:25.085 --> 01:26.419
Maybe it's for you.

01:26.503 --> 01:28.963
- It wasn't for her.
- No, it's them over there.

01:29.047 --> 01:32.425
- Let's celebrate.
- It's so pretty. What a lucky girl.

01:33.259 --> 01:35.845
- Look at the ring.
- Beautiful.

01:35.929 --> 01:39.432
Soo-jin, will you marry me?

01:39.516 --> 01:44.395
Say you will. Say you will.

01:44.479 --> 01:47.982
Marriage always felt
like a natural progression for me.

01:49.359 --> 01:54.489
Just like how the flowers bloom in spring
and the rainy season comes in summer,

01:55.115 --> 01:58.910
it felt natural,
something that would just come.

01:58.993 --> 02:00.537
Summer heat is in full swing,

02:00.620 --> 02:03.248
and the rainy season's
just around the corner.

02:03.331 --> 02:05.875
Cloudy skies can be expected
starting this weekend

02:05.959 --> 02:07.293
with some ongoing showers…

02:07.377 --> 02:09.420
However, with climate change

02:09.504 --> 02:12.841
and the growing uncertainty
of weather forecasting nowadays…

02:14.300 --> 02:15.677
Why did they take a risk like that?

02:15.760 --> 02:16.678
Huh?

02:16.761 --> 02:18.680
Wow, that's so sweet.

02:18.763 --> 02:21.933
- So cool.
- Oh, uh, it's noisy in here.

02:22.016 --> 02:23.476
- Should we leave now?
- Very nice.

02:23.560 --> 02:25.270
- I love it. Ah!
- Okay.

02:27.814 --> 02:31.693
What really is natural
to us anymore?

02:32.610 --> 02:33.987
No way.

02:34.863 --> 02:36.573
How could it even happen?

02:36.656 --> 02:38.950
Those two are together?

02:39.450 --> 02:41.286
Are you sure you're not confused about it?

02:41.369 --> 02:43.079
I saw it with my own two eyes.

02:43.163 --> 02:46.207
The two of them were driving around
and went in for a drink.

02:46.291 --> 02:47.709
Well, they're on the same team.

02:47.792 --> 02:49.294
Of course, coworkers go for drinks.

02:49.377 --> 02:52.672
Also, what's her name? Jin Ha-kyung.
She's not his type at all.

02:52.755 --> 02:53.965
Same thing with Ha-kyung.

02:54.048 --> 02:56.801
She'd never go for a guy
who is that arrogant and headstrong.

02:56.885 --> 02:58.303
That's what I'm saying.

02:58.386 --> 03:00.889
I just don't think it makes sense
that they would be going out, huh?

03:14.903 --> 03:16.487
I'm sure that he's just, uh,

03:16.571 --> 03:19.032
going after her
to get back at me, that bastard.

03:19.115 --> 03:20.658
What?

03:21.242 --> 03:24.621
Si-woo oppa is unpredictable,
but he wouldn't do something like that.

03:26.456 --> 03:27.540
"Oppa"?

03:28.333 --> 03:30.293
You just called that guy your oppa?

03:32.420 --> 03:34.464
I misspoke. I take it back.

03:35.340 --> 03:37.175
Anyway, that's not like Lee Si-woo.

03:38.468 --> 03:41.679
Uh-huh. And I bet
he wouldn't do this either.

03:41.763 --> 03:43.389
Look what he did. What he did here.

03:43.473 --> 03:46.142
- That's because you attacked him first.
- I told you.

03:46.643 --> 03:48.394
Never take his side over mine, didn't I?

03:51.522 --> 03:52.774
What? What?

03:52.857 --> 03:54.234
What's on your mind?

03:56.402 --> 03:59.447
I'm saying those two are not dating.

04:00.156 --> 04:03.201
So stop dragging other people
into our relationship, oppa.

04:04.035 --> 04:07.622
- Seriously.
- Come on. He's trying to hurt me.

04:07.705 --> 04:09.499
I'm serious! I know!

04:17.966 --> 04:19.342
Uh, in the restaurant--

04:19.425 --> 04:21.552
What should we do this weekend?

04:21.636 --> 04:23.638
- Huh?
- We're off duty.

04:23.721 --> 04:25.181
What do you want to do?

04:25.765 --> 04:27.892
Ah, I don't know.

04:28.810 --> 04:31.271
Hmm, we could see a movie.

04:31.354 --> 04:34.023
Or, uh, that horror one
looked pretty cool, so…

04:35.108 --> 04:36.150
Sure.

04:37.527 --> 04:39.612
Maybe we could drive out to the suburbs.

04:40.280 --> 04:41.698
That sounds good too.

04:41.781 --> 04:43.992
Or do you wanna work out together?

04:44.075 --> 04:45.827
Seems like you like to run too.

04:46.327 --> 04:47.328
Also great.

04:49.247 --> 04:52.917
Or we could just get
some groceries from the market.

04:53.543 --> 04:54.377
Okay.

04:55.795 --> 04:59.549
- You're saying okay to everything.
- Hmm?

04:59.632 --> 05:01.134
You don't sound excited.

05:01.759 --> 05:04.929
You're just saying yes to whatever I say.

05:05.013 --> 05:07.390
That's because everything
really does sound good.

05:08.641 --> 05:10.685
To be honest,
I just like walking together.

05:11.269 --> 05:13.104
Well, I do too, yeah.

05:13.688 --> 05:16.733
But we don't get a lot of days off,
so I want us to do something special.

05:17.317 --> 05:18.526
So what's your preference?

05:19.110 --> 05:20.611
Um…

05:20.695 --> 05:22.530
There are a few options.

05:22.613 --> 05:25.616
I want to go check out one
of those rock and roll bowling places.

05:25.700 --> 05:28.286
And I want to go to Jeju Island for--

05:28.369 --> 05:31.080
Let's forget that. There will be
too many newlyweds there

05:31.164 --> 05:32.206
this time of the year.

05:32.874 --> 05:34.125
What's wrong with newlyweds?

05:34.709 --> 05:35.793
I don't know.

05:36.669 --> 05:37.754
It's suffocating?

05:38.463 --> 05:39.672
What do you mean?

05:39.756 --> 05:44.093
That, uh, whole thing of marriage
being the end goal, it's not always right.

05:44.177 --> 05:48.514
When I see married people acting
like now, it's all happily ever after.

05:51.309 --> 05:53.102
Well, it's different for everyone.

05:53.686 --> 05:56.522
But still, I just feel
a little suffocated.

05:59.484 --> 06:02.070
Oh, hang here.
I'll go get us some cold drinks.

06:02.153 --> 06:04.364
- Hmm.
- Okay.

06:14.874 --> 06:20.463
EPISODE 9
DRY CHANGMA (RAINY SEASON)

06:20.546 --> 06:23.216
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

06:26.260 --> 06:29.222
A stationary front has currently formed
over the southern Jeju Sea.

06:29.305 --> 06:32.475
It seems like it will start raining
in Jeju early tomorrow now.

06:33.476 --> 06:38.606
The stationary front is moving
along about how we expected at 35km/h.

06:39.899 --> 06:41.359
- Thirty-five kilometers?
- Yes.

06:42.985 --> 06:45.947
Judging
by the current situation in the air,

06:46.030 --> 06:49.617
rainfall will start in the metro area
tomorrow evening as expected.

06:49.700 --> 06:51.786
- That's right, sir.
- Hmm.

06:53.246 --> 06:55.289
- How about the press?
- Uh, yes.

06:55.373 --> 06:56.874
Because of the heat wave,

06:56.958 --> 06:58.876
the rainy season
has everyone very excited.

06:58.960 --> 06:59.919
I see.

07:00.670 --> 07:01.921
Okay, good.

07:02.004 --> 07:05.091
We'll give the press the briefing
as planned. Let's move on.

07:05.174 --> 07:08.010
Yes, sir. Hello, Jeju Office?

07:10.930 --> 07:12.390
All right.

07:12.473 --> 07:13.683
Great job, everyone.

07:13.766 --> 07:15.768
Thank you!

07:15.852 --> 07:18.938
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

07:29.031 --> 07:30.199
May I have a word with you?

07:47.842 --> 07:49.218
Are you dating Lee Si-woo?

07:51.137 --> 07:52.096
What?

07:52.805 --> 07:53.890
Am I dating who?

07:53.973 --> 07:55.933
I saw everything. I saw you together.

07:56.809 --> 07:59.562
The place I told you
that's a good spot to go have a drink.

07:59.645 --> 08:01.272
The Izakaya, I saw you two.

08:03.608 --> 08:05.359
Ah, that night.

08:06.068 --> 08:08.154
Lee Si-woo and I are teammates.

08:08.237 --> 08:10.031
Can't a couple of teammates
go for a drink?

08:10.114 --> 08:12.033
- That looks like dating to you, huh?
- Nu-uh.

08:12.533 --> 08:15.161
Your mouth on his
is what looks like dating.

08:16.746 --> 08:18.164
What? Come on!

08:18.247 --> 08:21.584
You've really changed, Jin Ha-kyung.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.795
When we dated, you used to hate showing
any affection when others were around.

08:24.879 --> 08:27.423
And now you're out there going around
kissing Lee Si-woo

08:27.507 --> 08:28.758
where the whole bar can see you.

08:30.968 --> 08:33.888
You… I should have known since that day.

08:34.472 --> 08:36.140
When I was fighting with him,

08:37.099 --> 08:40.436
I thought it was weird you left together,
so I followed to see where you went.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.230
You were having a real moment.

08:42.313 --> 08:43.439
Then…

08:43.940 --> 08:44.982
Am I supposed to do nothing

08:45.066 --> 08:46.859
if my subordinates get beat up
by some psycho?

08:46.943 --> 08:49.904
A psycho who I was involved with
in the past?

08:49.987 --> 08:51.322
- "Psycho"?
- What of it, huh?

08:51.405 --> 08:53.407
Why would I ever want to date
in the workplace again

08:53.491 --> 08:55.910
after what you and I went through?
Are you crazy?

08:56.494 --> 08:57.995
- What--
- Also…

08:59.539 --> 09:02.792
Why do you even care
who I'm kissing or making out with?

09:03.834 --> 09:05.002
- Hey!
- What?

09:06.003 --> 09:07.213
I'm scared for you, 'kay?

09:08.047 --> 09:09.674
Men know what men can do.

09:09.757 --> 09:12.260
Lee Si-woo is not a decent guy.

09:12.343 --> 09:15.221
Also, I didn't want to bring this up.

09:15.304 --> 09:18.391
But do you even know what kind of scene
he made at my wedding with Yu-jin?

09:18.474 --> 09:21.727
Ah, so you broke off our wedding
with everything planned

09:21.811 --> 09:24.021
to marry another woman
because you're such a good guy?

09:24.105 --> 09:27.066
Oh, gosh, look, okay?
Yu-jin gave me no choice.

09:27.149 --> 09:29.735
That bastard is just trying to get
his revenge on me through you.

09:29.819 --> 09:32.113
Oh, so you're just really concerned,
then, huh?

09:32.196 --> 09:33.447
Of course, I'm concerned.

09:33.531 --> 09:35.658
The only thing you're scared off
is your name getting dragged

09:35.741 --> 09:37.702
through the dirt
if I go out with Lee Si-woo.

09:37.785 --> 09:39.954
Well, of course, yeah, that too.

09:40.037 --> 09:41.872
Be honest. Wouldn't you be scared of that?

09:43.583 --> 09:44.875
- Hey!
- What?

09:44.959 --> 09:46.043
Go to hell.

09:51.299 --> 09:53.217
Ha-kyung, you can't do this!

09:53.301 --> 09:54.802
Ha-kyung, hey!

09:56.345 --> 09:59.265
She's got no sense at all.

10:14.697 --> 10:17.199
It's revenge! I'm serious!

10:40.598 --> 10:43.893
Aren't you excited for the weekend, huh?

10:44.477 --> 10:47.772
Of course.
It's my first weekend in forever.

10:47.855 --> 10:50.816
I can't ever see anybody
on a weekday when I'm off.

10:50.900 --> 10:52.568
It's so lonely.

10:54.236 --> 10:56.656
I wish I could have
a little loneliness on my day off.

10:56.739 --> 10:59.867
Just kids. Kids all the time,
whenever I get a weekend.

10:59.950 --> 11:01.410
And if they've got study sessions,

11:01.494 --> 11:03.788
I have to take them back
and forth all over town.

11:04.372 --> 11:05.665
I'd rather be right here.

11:06.415 --> 11:07.416
Mm.

11:10.878 --> 11:13.422
I already know what Mr. Um's gonna do.

11:16.384 --> 11:18.427
What are you doing tomorrow, Mr. Lee?

11:19.053 --> 11:21.013
I've got a date, so…

11:21.097 --> 11:22.973
I heard that a good play opened.

11:23.057 --> 11:25.351
Oh, I love theater. What show is it?

11:25.434 --> 11:27.728
Oh, uh… What was it?

11:28.729 --> 11:31.065
- Emergency.
- "Emergency"?

11:31.148 --> 11:32.441
"Emergency"?

11:33.025 --> 11:34.735
- Oh, the show?
- Huh?

11:34.819 --> 11:37.530
Oh, uh, it's a musical at a small theater.

11:37.613 --> 11:39.156
Oh, a small theater.

11:39.240 --> 11:41.075
What is it?

11:42.410 --> 11:44.245
And you, Mr. Shin? Your weekend?

11:44.328 --> 11:47.289
Well, a weekend off
doesn't change anything.

11:47.998 --> 11:51.377
- First, when I get up, I make a coffee.
- Hmm.

11:51.460 --> 11:53.379
Han Ki-jun is onto us.

11:55.214 --> 11:56.173
How?

11:56.882 --> 11:59.885
He saw us together
at the Izakaya that day.

12:01.387 --> 12:03.222
So what did you say?

12:04.640 --> 12:06.392
I denied it, of course.

12:11.063 --> 12:14.191
For breakfast,
I usually have a simple salad.

12:15.234 --> 12:18.696
Work out and try
and clean up around the house.

12:18.779 --> 12:22.783
Or maybe
why don't we just come clean?

12:22.867 --> 12:24.535
We have to keep denying it.

12:25.661 --> 12:27.371
I eat the food when it comes.

12:27.955 --> 12:29.832
And after lunch, I put on a record…

12:29.915 --> 12:32.251
Let's not go
to Daehangno tomorrow.

12:34.628 --> 12:35.963
Why not?

12:36.046 --> 12:38.674
There's a maeundalgbaljib place
Ki-jun really likes there.

12:38.758 --> 12:42.136
He goes there sometimes,
so I think tomorrow is too risky.

12:42.219 --> 12:44.597
…classical pianists have
different brain structures.

12:44.680 --> 12:45.681
Actually…

12:45.765 --> 12:47.558
It wasn't easy
to get those tickets.

12:47.641 --> 12:49.685
Should we go for a jog near Hangang, then?

12:49.769 --> 12:51.687
When they need a jazz pianist…

12:51.771 --> 12:54.982
No. We shouldn't
go outside at all for a while.

12:56.525 --> 12:58.360
We can't just stay home.

12:58.444 --> 12:59.904
The biggest difference was that

12:59.987 --> 13:01.864
the jazz pianists showed
high reactive brains

13:01.947 --> 13:04.200
and the classical pianists
showed high accuracy.

13:04.283 --> 13:06.202
It's fascinating.

13:06.285 --> 13:10.831
They're both interesting, depending
on the perfect opportunity to focus on.

13:10.915 --> 13:14.043
Their brainwaves have
physical reactions differently.

13:14.126 --> 13:15.920
So maybe it's the same for us?

13:16.545 --> 13:20.424
We're all forecasters,
but for digital forecasters…

13:22.843 --> 13:26.013
CONTINUOUS HEAT WAVE…
JIN HA-KYUNG?

13:26.096 --> 13:29.183
Yu-jin, do you know
who Lee Si-woo is dating right now?

13:29.767 --> 13:30.768
Who is he dating?

13:31.352 --> 13:32.436
Jin Ha-kyung.

13:34.355 --> 13:35.981
Makes no sense.

13:36.065 --> 13:38.067
- What?
- Huh?

13:38.150 --> 13:40.694
- What makes no sense?
- Nothing, I'm good.

13:42.404 --> 13:44.031
MOTHER-IN-LAW

14:02.049 --> 14:04.802
Hi, eomeoni. How are you?

14:07.513 --> 14:08.556
Sorry?

14:09.849 --> 14:13.686
Ah. Oh, so sorry. Um, I forgot.

14:13.769 --> 14:15.855
Uh, yes, I'll tell Ki-jun.

14:17.606 --> 14:18.649
Okay.

14:19.567 --> 14:21.944
Well, I'll see you this weekend.

14:22.027 --> 14:23.195
Yes.

14:38.919 --> 14:41.380
- Where are you going?
- Uh, shopping errand.

14:41.463 --> 14:42.381
"Shopping"?

14:43.257 --> 14:45.759
Door is opening.

14:52.641 --> 14:54.476
- Door is closing.
- Hey, eonni.

14:55.269 --> 14:57.688
Mom said you should drop by
on your way home today.

14:57.771 --> 14:59.231
Um, I'm busy.

15:02.234 --> 15:05.404
She's going to go to your place
if you don't come over here.

15:06.363 --> 15:07.865
- I'm sure she will--
- Si-woo.

15:07.948 --> 15:09.366
What should we do for dinner?

15:10.075 --> 15:12.953
- Budaejjigae sounds good.
- You know how to make it?

15:13.037 --> 15:15.497
- Okay. I'll be right there.
- No. I know how to order it, though.

15:17.583 --> 15:21.045
- That's strange.
- What? She's not coming here?

15:22.338 --> 15:24.340
- She's on her way.
- Huh?

15:25.341 --> 15:26.342
Ma.

15:26.425 --> 15:28.135
Are you really gonna confront Ha-kyung?

15:28.218 --> 15:29.261
Just leave her alone.

15:29.345 --> 15:31.680
That is not what parents do.

15:36.101 --> 15:38.687
What else should we add?

15:38.771 --> 15:40.564
- Dumplings.
- Dumplings? All right.

15:40.648 --> 15:42.650
- Yeah, and we have ramen at home.
- We do have ramen.

15:42.733 --> 15:45.986
Ooh, we're gonna order, uh, budaejjigae.
Is there anything we should add to that?

15:46.070 --> 15:49.865
Uh, well, I got to go to my mom's house,
so you two enjoy dinner.

15:50.866 --> 15:51.867
Your mom's?

15:53.452 --> 15:55.496
- Is something, uh…
- I don't know.

16:04.588 --> 16:06.715
You know the school trip
I need for credit?

16:07.549 --> 16:08.968
Where should I go this time?

16:10.928 --> 16:12.012
Where are you?

16:12.096 --> 16:13.889
At the KMA, like always.

16:13.973 --> 16:15.724
He's not here. He left a while ago.

16:18.394 --> 16:20.562
Where on earth
has he been sleeping these days?

16:23.357 --> 16:24.274
Eomma?

16:26.026 --> 16:26.902
Huh?

16:27.486 --> 16:29.530
It's okay. I can handle it.

16:31.156 --> 16:33.200
- What is it?
- The school trip.

16:37.871 --> 16:39.164
I have one idea.

16:42.042 --> 16:44.795
Go on just three blind dates
that I arranged.

16:45.462 --> 16:47.756
That's my final wish.

16:47.840 --> 16:50.217
Come on, Ha-kyung. Just do it.

16:51.885 --> 16:53.262
I said no from the start.

16:53.762 --> 16:55.472
Am I supposed to throw away money
for nothing?

16:55.556 --> 16:57.891
What about my time, huh?
Should I throw that out?

16:58.684 --> 17:02.271
That's the reason I said
only three dates and no more.

17:03.564 --> 17:06.442
Who knows? Maybe on one of those,
you'll meet the man for you.

17:07.026 --> 17:10.654
These days, they say couples
who met this way

17:10.738 --> 17:14.366
get divorced far less than those
who just met through dating.

17:15.159 --> 17:17.411
Why look at me?

17:17.494 --> 17:18.829
Passion and drama?

17:18.912 --> 17:21.373
All of that's no good at all.

17:21.457 --> 17:22.875
Just look at Tae-kyung.

17:22.958 --> 17:24.960
They acted like
they'd die without each other,

17:25.044 --> 17:26.545
and then one year
after the wedding, divorce.

17:26.628 --> 17:28.714
Mom, why do you always say that?

17:28.797 --> 17:30.507
It's about her, not me!

17:34.428 --> 17:37.514
Don't try and wait
to pay me respect once I'm gone.

17:37.598 --> 17:40.601
There's still time for that now, huh?

17:41.727 --> 17:43.062
While I'm living.

17:53.030 --> 17:55.574
You cold-hearted brat!

17:56.241 --> 17:58.452
It's the last wish
of your old mother, huh?

17:58.535 --> 18:01.872
Is it really that hard?
How can you just say no?

18:01.955 --> 18:03.082
Listen!

18:03.707 --> 18:05.292
How can you just strike me down

18:05.375 --> 18:08.128
without the slightest hesitation, huh?
Huh?

18:08.212 --> 18:11.673
I'm sick of always hearing about marriage.
What? Are they arresting singles?

18:11.757 --> 18:14.093
Oh! Oh! That little…

18:15.385 --> 18:18.180
- I'm leaving.
- You're being too harsh.

18:19.598 --> 18:22.351
You know she's just acting like that
'cause she's frustrated.

18:22.434 --> 18:24.895
You and I are the only kids she has.

18:26.021 --> 18:30.526
Her eldest came crawling to her,
a failed wife, and her youngest…

18:30.609 --> 18:32.111
She just wants to know that

18:32.194 --> 18:34.655
you and I'll have someone to lean on
when she goes.

18:35.572 --> 18:37.574
Come on, that's all she wants.

18:39.827 --> 18:42.079
Well, then, Mom can remarry.
Oh! Or you could.

18:42.162 --> 18:44.748
Hey, watch your manners.

18:46.375 --> 18:48.752
Do you know how I feel
every time it goes like this?

18:49.336 --> 18:51.880
I feel like I'm being pushed
to the edge of a cliff.

18:51.964 --> 18:55.884
And how come it always feels that way?
It makes me feel so angry.

18:57.719 --> 18:59.930
Yeah. You got a point.

19:01.598 --> 19:04.101
Anyway, I… I feel awful. I'm heading out.

19:29.168 --> 19:30.210
Ma.

19:32.588 --> 19:34.840
Were you happy
when you and Dad were together?

19:36.383 --> 19:39.136
Why would you go and ask me that
out of nowhere?

19:40.220 --> 19:42.931
There's not one marriage that's just good.

19:43.015 --> 19:45.559
Sometimes it's simple.
And sometimes it's not.

19:46.310 --> 19:51.732
Despite that, two is better than one,
and three is much better than two.

19:51.815 --> 19:52.983
You know Mi-jeong.

19:53.066 --> 19:56.028
Her daughter would use to say
she'd live alone forever.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.529
But look now.

19:57.613 --> 20:00.490
Now she's got a great life.
A husband and kids too.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.285
And her husband's got a good job.

20:05.454 --> 20:08.707
But you have to understand
Ha-kyung's not the same as her.

20:10.334 --> 20:11.960
Maybe living alone really works for her.

20:12.544 --> 20:13.378
What?

20:15.422 --> 20:18.300
Well, it's worth considering at least.

20:20.344 --> 20:24.223
Go to bed. All that yelling this evening
must have tired you out.

20:36.610 --> 20:37.694
Oh, hey.

20:39.696 --> 20:40.781
Hey.

20:42.115 --> 20:43.367
Your mom called today.

20:46.787 --> 20:48.914
She wants to have dinner with us tomorrow.

20:49.539 --> 20:50.916
You're free, aren't you?

20:52.542 --> 20:53.961
Did you go shopping again?

20:55.170 --> 20:57.714
- Oh, uh, that's--
- Must be nice to be so carefree.

20:57.798 --> 21:00.050
I thought we were saving money
'cause of our lease.

21:01.218 --> 21:04.096
We can afford the deposit
for the new place thanks to the loan.

21:04.179 --> 21:07.099
But you know it's not cheap to move
and there's still a lot to take care of.

21:07.182 --> 21:10.811
Are you saying that I'm just
thoughtlessly spending our money?

21:11.770 --> 21:12.980
If you were being rational,

21:13.563 --> 21:15.774
you wouldn't have spent
our money like it's nothing.

21:15.857 --> 21:16.775
Oppa.

21:16.858 --> 21:18.151
Forget about it.

21:18.235 --> 21:19.903
It'll just become a fight if we talk.

21:21.029 --> 21:22.281
I gotta shower.

21:42.843 --> 21:44.386
Is something going on at home?

21:50.517 --> 21:51.768
Yeah.

21:51.852 --> 21:54.187
But you don't have to worry about it.

21:59.026 --> 22:00.360
If you're tired,

22:00.444 --> 22:03.405
I'm fine with just chilling
at the apartment tomorrow.

22:09.578 --> 22:11.997
Will you look out the living room
in a second?

22:20.213 --> 22:21.173
Want a beer?

22:25.469 --> 22:27.763
Uh, no, all for you.

22:27.846 --> 22:29.598
Mm-hmm.

22:42.319 --> 22:45.197
Yeah, staying here
is not really an option.

22:45.280 --> 22:46.323
Is it?

22:46.406 --> 22:48.867
Let's just avoid
crowded places.

22:50.702 --> 22:53.580
A place where it's less crowded
when it rains.

22:53.663 --> 22:55.415
Can you think of a place like that?

22:58.460 --> 23:01.088
There is one place
I can think of.

23:02.130 --> 23:04.549
- Where?
- Do you like nature?

23:05.509 --> 23:06.718
Of course.

23:08.387 --> 23:10.555
Can you stand
a little inconvenience?

23:14.559 --> 23:16.019
I guess.

23:16.853 --> 23:18.021
Okay, then.

23:21.483 --> 23:24.361
Where are we going?

23:46.716 --> 23:49.052
What are you doing, huh?

24:17.247 --> 24:18.957
You're off work today, right?

24:19.040 --> 24:20.500
I need to talk to you.

24:20.584 --> 24:22.919
Meet me at the brunch café
in front of the apartment when you get up.

24:23.003 --> 24:24.212
I'll be waiting.

24:34.639 --> 24:36.266
Hmm?

24:47.611 --> 24:48.778
Morning.

24:48.862 --> 24:50.655
Lee Si-woo.

24:50.739 --> 24:52.365
- Thanks for waiting
- Shall we?

24:52.449 --> 24:55.035
What? Director and subordinate together?

24:57.370 --> 24:59.331
You two are busted.

25:31.488 --> 25:33.323
Where the hell are they going?

25:50.799 --> 25:52.050
HONEY

25:52.133 --> 25:55.178
Where are you? You didn't forget
that we're visiting your mom, right?

25:55.262 --> 25:58.265
We need to leave before six,
so be home by then.

25:58.348 --> 26:00.767
All right. I got time. I got time.

26:03.144 --> 26:04.688
Traffic looks lighter.

26:05.313 --> 26:07.732
- So where are we going?
- We're almost there.

26:09.818 --> 26:12.946
I hope you'll enjoy it.

26:36.511 --> 26:37.846
- Thank you.
- It's right up there.

26:37.929 --> 26:39.889
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

26:52.777 --> 26:54.487
What?

26:56.656 --> 26:58.283
Who let their dog…

26:59.534 --> 27:01.953
You little…

27:02.537 --> 27:05.415
Oh, jeez.

27:08.752 --> 27:12.339
HONEY

27:19.262 --> 27:20.639
This is so nice.

27:22.891 --> 27:24.017
I'm so glad we came here.

27:24.100 --> 27:25.143
Here, I'll help with that.

27:25.226 --> 27:26.561
No, it's okay.

27:40.283 --> 27:42.869
How come he's ghosting me all of a sudden?

27:55.548 --> 27:58.468
The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

28:08.478 --> 28:11.189
We're here
at Camp Site Letter B.

28:11.773 --> 28:13.566
So we need to go that way.

28:13.650 --> 28:15.110
Oh, that's a long walk.

28:15.777 --> 28:18.530
- Oh, it's no problem. Let's go.
- Okay.

28:19.906 --> 28:21.241
- Can I help?
- No, thanks.

28:21.324 --> 28:22.867
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

28:22.951 --> 28:23.910
Let's go.

28:24.494 --> 28:26.538
I'll hop on. You're so strong.

28:26.621 --> 28:28.873
Are you riding it? Then I'll push.

28:28.957 --> 28:31.584
I'll make irrefutable evidence
when I confront them.

28:33.878 --> 28:35.797
Uh… Uh…

28:36.923 --> 28:37.924
Where is it?

28:38.591 --> 28:40.593
All right. I got time. I got time. Yeah.

28:44.597 --> 28:48.143
Ah!

28:50.186 --> 28:51.187
What do I do?

29:22.886 --> 29:23.887
Hmm…

29:33.438 --> 29:34.606
Did she go out?

29:35.857 --> 29:37.817
Si-woo, you had breakfast yet?

29:39.068 --> 29:41.696
Hmm. How about we go get, um…

29:43.948 --> 29:46.868
Where is everyone?

30:00.340 --> 30:01.841
MOBILE DISASTER PREVENTION
AND WEATHER SYSTEM

30:01.925 --> 30:02.759
NO CONNECTION

30:09.098 --> 30:11.100
That's weird. I can't get a signal.

30:11.184 --> 30:12.644
Internet's not working?

30:13.228 --> 30:14.062
Yeah.

30:14.145 --> 30:16.314
They definitely said it would.

30:16.397 --> 30:18.525
It'd be great to at least see
the live reporting.

30:20.693 --> 30:21.986
Hang on a second.

30:24.697 --> 30:26.074
- Hey.
- Hello.

30:26.658 --> 30:29.369
Could you check
the current situation on the live radar?

30:29.953 --> 30:31.663
You can do it yourself.

30:33.039 --> 30:35.375
I'm outside and I don't have any internet.

30:36.125 --> 30:37.252
Just do it for a friend?

30:39.003 --> 30:43.132
You have to be joking. Wait a second.

30:43.216 --> 30:44.050
What's…

30:44.133 --> 30:46.469
Oh, he's going over to…
Let me see your phone.

30:47.470 --> 30:52.851
Right now, the stationary front
is moving northward Jeju 5mm of rain.

30:52.934 --> 30:55.019
And it's barely drizzling
on the south coast.

30:55.103 --> 30:56.396
Okay.

30:57.730 --> 31:00.608
It's drizzling in Jeju
and the southern region.

31:03.111 --> 31:04.362
Just a second, Seok-ho.

31:04.946 --> 31:07.323
Also ask
for the NWP model from 1:00 p.m.

31:07.407 --> 31:09.784
Oh, the NWP model too?

31:11.452 --> 31:12.704
Who are you with right now?

31:17.000 --> 31:18.751
With my girlfriend.

31:22.547 --> 31:26.384
Then forget about this stuff
and just enjoy your date.

31:27.010 --> 31:30.513
Team One's in the office, and I'll keep
an eye on the live situation.

31:30.597 --> 31:32.390
- I'm hanging up.
- Okay.

31:36.686 --> 31:37.854
What did he say?

31:38.646 --> 31:43.526
He said there's lots of people at the KMA,
so I should focus on what I'm doing.

31:44.444 --> 31:46.613
I know that already. I'm just curious.

31:46.696 --> 31:48.114
Seok-ho is right.

31:48.197 --> 31:50.742
We need to relax, so we can be rested.

31:50.825 --> 31:53.870
The stationary front
is heading north as expected.

31:53.953 --> 31:56.414
So just forget it.
Let's focus on each other.

31:57.665 --> 31:58.708
Okay.

32:03.004 --> 32:04.297
- This, then?
- Yeah.

32:26.611 --> 32:27.737
Okay.

32:28.363 --> 32:29.405
Right.

32:30.031 --> 32:31.866
Team One will take care of it.

32:33.284 --> 32:35.286
Okay, forget it. All right.

32:43.044 --> 32:45.797
One vanilla latte, please.
Some soy milk, please.

32:45.880 --> 32:47.465
And just two pumps of syrup. No more.

32:47.548 --> 32:49.092
I'll use my free one.

32:49.676 --> 32:52.095
- What's your name?
- It's Shin Seok-ho.

32:57.433 --> 32:58.351
There's no card.

32:59.560 --> 33:01.896
What do you mean there's no card?
I just got my last…

33:02.480 --> 33:05.316
- From who?
- I don't know. A staff member.

33:05.400 --> 33:07.777
Yeah. I'm getting a coffee first.

33:07.860 --> 33:10.738
When our manager comes in,
she can check for you, okay?

33:10.822 --> 33:12.198
Can you just pay for it now?

33:12.782 --> 33:15.660
So you're saying
my punch card is lost now?

33:16.244 --> 33:18.955
I let you people keep it
because you said it would be safe.

33:21.249 --> 33:23.418
Oh, 1302?

33:24.961 --> 33:26.462
Other customers are waiting right now.

33:26.546 --> 33:28.506
Right, how about we check one more time?

33:37.640 --> 33:38.850
Hello.

33:38.933 --> 33:40.893
Oh, what brings you here?

33:42.061 --> 33:43.896
This is a coffee shop.
I'm here for coffee.

33:43.980 --> 33:44.939
Right.

33:45.023 --> 33:47.650
What about you? What… what's going on?

33:48.860 --> 33:51.362
They lost my card
with all 12 stamps on it.

33:52.697 --> 33:54.323
The one they stored?

33:55.033 --> 33:59.787
As I was saying, he must understand
we can't confirm the stamps right now.

33:59.871 --> 34:02.457
I'll look into this
when my manager arrives, okay?

34:02.540 --> 34:04.042
So, please, for now, if you could pay--

34:04.125 --> 34:06.252
I didn't bring my wallet
because I had a full card.

34:07.045 --> 34:09.589
- So should I cancel your order, then?
- Ridiculous.

34:10.173 --> 34:12.300
- Here, you can put it on this one.
- No, you don't have to.

34:12.383 --> 34:14.469
I owe you from the other day.

34:15.386 --> 34:16.763
What's your order?

34:18.056 --> 34:22.185
A vanilla latte, some soy milk,
and just two pumps of syrup, no more.

34:23.227 --> 34:26.230
Ah! Okay, that. And I'll have
a cold, iced Americano, please.

34:26.314 --> 34:27.690
You can put his on here.

34:29.484 --> 34:30.735
Um…

34:31.903 --> 34:35.114
So saying "cold, iced Americano,"
that's redundant, see,

34:35.198 --> 34:38.409
because if they make it with ice,
it has to be cold, so…

34:42.497 --> 34:45.249
- Don't you think that I'd know that?
- Right.

34:47.460 --> 34:49.170
- Oh, and thank you.
- Okay.

34:51.214 --> 34:52.381
Mm, thanks.

34:54.175 --> 34:55.384
Go ahead.

34:58.763 --> 35:01.974
One chamomile tea, please.

35:10.399 --> 35:12.819
No, wait! Hold on! Hey!

35:12.902 --> 35:14.070
Hey, my car!

35:14.153 --> 35:15.655
My car! My car!

35:15.738 --> 35:18.699
Hey! Wait! Stop

35:19.826 --> 35:20.827
Hey!

35:27.959 --> 35:28.876
What?

35:29.877 --> 35:31.295
It's bothering me.

35:33.131 --> 35:34.590
It will rain, right?

35:35.633 --> 35:36.884
Don't you think so?

35:37.552 --> 35:40.138
Of course. Look how gray the clouds are.

35:40.721 --> 35:41.931
It'll rain.

35:52.567 --> 35:53.526
Hey.

35:58.364 --> 36:00.158
I know you're curious too.

36:01.075 --> 36:03.870
Well, then, let's try something.
Hand me your phone.

36:06.038 --> 36:09.584
Okay. Whoever takes their phone first
does the dishes.

36:11.377 --> 36:13.045
Sure, but…

36:13.629 --> 36:15.965
…shouldn't we cook something
before we worry about the dishes?

36:16.841 --> 36:19.677
Camping requires barbecue.

36:19.760 --> 36:21.846
All right. Yeah.

36:22.513 --> 36:24.515
What you got?

36:25.850 --> 36:26.934
Huh?

36:27.810 --> 36:30.897
Huh? What?

36:31.606 --> 36:32.732
Why, what is it?

36:35.359 --> 36:37.987
Meat. I definitely put it in here.

37:12.146 --> 37:13.689
It's okay.

37:13.773 --> 37:15.858
Camping always needs kimchi-jjigae.

37:16.442 --> 37:17.985
We don't have anything for the broth.

37:19.695 --> 37:21.989
Should I go get some beef
from the store over there?

37:22.073 --> 37:24.075
All we need for kimchi-jjigae is kimchi.

37:28.412 --> 37:30.164
It's okay.

37:51.102 --> 37:53.562
- How is it, uh, looking?
- It's okay.

37:53.646 --> 37:55.856
- Is it good?
- I don't know.

37:55.940 --> 37:57.275
I haven't tasted it.

37:57.942 --> 37:59.902
- Wow, you're good at this.
- Okay, try it.

37:59.986 --> 38:01.404
- Try it?
- Mm-hmm.

38:04.407 --> 38:05.408
Mmm.

38:05.491 --> 38:06.826
- Very good.
- Is it good?

38:06.909 --> 38:08.160
Here, try it.

38:11.330 --> 38:13.457
- Hmm?
- Wow, I think I'm a genius.

38:13.541 --> 38:16.252
- It's so good.
- Stay. Oh, oh, hold it.

38:17.712 --> 38:20.923
VEHICLES SUBJECT TO FINES AND TOWS

38:26.971 --> 38:29.223
HONEY

38:30.266 --> 38:32.393
- Hey.
- Where are you?

38:33.728 --> 38:36.022
- Oh, uh, Yu-jin…
- I'll go straight to your mom's place.

38:36.105 --> 38:37.565
I'll see you there, okay?

38:37.648 --> 38:38.858
You have to hurry.

39:10.514 --> 39:11.932
Where are you coming from?

39:13.309 --> 39:14.810
And why are you so ragged?

39:16.062 --> 39:17.646
It's a long story.

39:19.023 --> 39:20.691
Did you forget what day it was?

39:21.359 --> 39:23.152
Your mom's birthday.

39:23.235 --> 39:25.988
You're so… cold-hearted.

39:26.072 --> 39:27.365
"Your mom"? Really?

39:27.948 --> 39:29.408
She's your mother-in-law, okay?

39:29.492 --> 39:30.618
You should call her "Mom."

39:31.202 --> 39:33.954
She called two days ago to make sure
that we could have dinner with her.

39:34.830 --> 39:36.332
Where were you all day?

39:36.874 --> 39:38.793
Do you know how awkward
it was alone with her?

39:40.878 --> 39:42.671
Did she say something to you again?

39:43.255 --> 39:45.257
Okay, I asked where you were!

39:45.341 --> 39:47.718
I'm old enough to go places
without your permission.

39:48.427 --> 39:51.931
Come on. I had something important
I had to check out.

39:52.014 --> 39:53.516
And now…

39:53.599 --> 39:56.811
Please don't say
you saw Jin Ha-kyung again.

39:59.146 --> 40:02.441
You said you couldn't believe
that Ha-kyung and that ass are dating.

40:02.525 --> 40:04.944
So she's just so important for you?

40:05.027 --> 40:07.279
So much so you forgot your mom's birthday?

40:08.948 --> 40:10.282
I don't know what to do.

40:10.366 --> 40:12.910
When I ended my engagement
with her and married you,

40:12.993 --> 40:14.662
do you know how much crap people gave me?

40:14.745 --> 40:17.456
They said I betrayed a woman
who'd stuck with me through thick and thin

40:17.540 --> 40:20.167
and that I'm a shameless cheat
who bailed at the last second.

40:20.751 --> 40:23.170
I had to go through all of that.

40:23.254 --> 40:26.215
I can't let her get away
with playing the victim

40:26.298 --> 40:28.759
when she's dating that bastard Lee Si-woo!

40:28.843 --> 40:29.802
Oppa.

40:29.885 --> 40:32.430
I really wish you'd focus on our problems.

40:32.513 --> 40:35.015
We have so much stuff
we need to fix together.

40:35.099 --> 40:36.642
I know.

40:36.725 --> 40:38.227
But I have to take care of this first

40:38.310 --> 40:40.646
before I can focus
on anything else, Yu-jin.

40:40.729 --> 40:41.897
So what will you do?

40:43.190 --> 40:44.650
Expose them to the whole world, huh?

40:44.733 --> 40:46.277
So what if I want to?

40:47.862 --> 40:49.196
You don't think

40:49.280 --> 40:51.157
that people will be talking about us too
if that got out?

40:51.240 --> 40:53.242
Why is it that you won't consider that?

40:57.663 --> 40:59.081
Be honest.

40:59.165 --> 41:01.542
I think you not wanting her
to play the victim is a cover.

41:01.625 --> 41:04.336
Aren't you just jealous of them
now that they're going out?

41:06.338 --> 41:07.298
"Jealous"?

41:07.381 --> 41:09.091
Me? Of Lee Si-woo?

41:09.175 --> 41:10.718
Why would I be?

41:10.801 --> 41:12.511
You're the one who would know that.

41:20.478 --> 41:21.520
I…

41:33.115 --> 41:34.325
It's not raining.

41:36.285 --> 41:37.369
I know.

41:43.959 --> 41:45.419
It's not going to, is it?

41:48.339 --> 41:49.548
Probably not.

41:51.133 --> 41:52.343
What's the time?

41:55.471 --> 41:57.723
It's going on 8:21.

41:59.767 --> 42:00.976
We're screwed.

42:03.062 --> 42:04.980
Cheers.

42:06.482 --> 42:07.483
Cheers.

42:12.613 --> 42:15.658
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

42:30.506 --> 42:31.757
Hmm…

42:38.055 --> 42:40.724
It's been over ten minutes
since the meeting started.

42:40.808 --> 42:43.060
Okay.

42:44.478 --> 42:47.565
I thought we saw the NWP
had moved northward.

42:48.399 --> 42:50.234
Hmm? Then why isn't it raining?

42:50.317 --> 42:52.486
The Okhotsk's anticyclone
is abnormally strong

42:52.570 --> 42:54.196
and the cold air
in the north isn't moving,

42:54.280 --> 42:57.032
so the northing of the stationary front
is being delayed.

42:57.908 --> 43:02.371
Isn't that the point that Mr. Um said
in our meeting before this, you know?

43:03.122 --> 43:04.290
Yeah.

43:09.128 --> 43:10.754
When is it going to rain?

43:10.838 --> 43:13.507
Right now, we're looking
at the start of next week.

43:13.591 --> 43:15.092
However, if this weather continues,

43:15.175 --> 43:17.761
we can't rule out the chance of it
taking even longer.

43:24.476 --> 43:25.769
Okay, then.

43:26.353 --> 43:29.023
PR should distribute explanations
to the press

43:29.106 --> 43:30.983
about why the rain has been delayed.

43:31.066 --> 43:33.319
And forecasting…

43:33.402 --> 43:35.779
…should stay focused on the live charts.

43:35.863 --> 43:37.031
Yes, sir.

43:37.114 --> 43:41.327
Wouldn't it be better if we mention
the possibility of a drier rainy season?

43:41.910 --> 43:43.787
- "Drier rainy season"?
- Yes.

43:44.288 --> 43:47.666
We can't do that
when the stationary front is still active.

43:48.292 --> 43:51.170
Even if it just stays cloudy
but doesn't rain,

43:51.253 --> 43:53.797
I don't think it's right to just rush
an announcement like that

43:53.881 --> 43:55.674
when rainfall's still likely.

44:00.054 --> 44:03.182
Isn't hasty conclusions
what you love? What?

44:03.265 --> 44:05.768
Your special sense isn't working so well
right now?

44:07.603 --> 44:12.149
Those senses are based on data
and the flow of the weather.

44:12.232 --> 44:13.942
Either it's right or it's not.

44:14.026 --> 44:15.653
We can't publish vague warnings

44:15.736 --> 44:18.072
just because we're afraid
of the criticism.

44:18.155 --> 44:19.948
"Publish vague warnings"?

44:20.032 --> 44:21.617
Isn't that what you were saying?

44:22.368 --> 44:23.661
Issue a statement?

44:29.958 --> 44:31.460
Please stop. Both of you.

44:31.543 --> 44:32.961
No, you go on.

44:33.045 --> 44:33.962
Huh?

44:34.922 --> 44:36.090
Please continue.

44:36.590 --> 44:38.967
Why don't you two gentlemen
debate it together?

44:39.051 --> 44:41.011
And then you can draw a joint conclusion.

44:41.095 --> 44:44.890
And we'll release the explanation material
to the news as a result of your findings.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.976
That would be great, right?
Right?

44:48.769 --> 44:49.978
Is there a problem?

44:51.105 --> 44:53.732
Uh, no, Director. We'll debate.

44:55.484 --> 44:57.486
Great. Carry on.

45:13.669 --> 45:14.962
Um, Director…

45:17.089 --> 45:18.924
I'm heading to that meeting.

45:19.007 --> 45:20.259
Will you survive?

45:20.968 --> 45:22.052
Yes.

46:00.048 --> 46:02.760
Let's start with analyzing
why the last forecast was wrong.

46:03.969 --> 46:05.888
I thought we were gonna work
on the reasons

46:05.971 --> 46:07.389
why the rainy season delay happened.

46:09.516 --> 46:12.060
I think we'd have to go back
to the forecast

46:12.144 --> 46:13.604
and find out what we missed,

46:13.687 --> 46:17.441
so we can explain the difference
between our prediction and what occurred.

46:21.612 --> 46:24.072
All right, sure. Where should we start?

46:28.327 --> 46:29.828
In the first set of forecast,

46:29.912 --> 46:32.456
you predicted the stationary front
would cause a rainfall starting

46:32.539 --> 46:35.292
in the Jeju area and the rest
of the southern region.

46:35.375 --> 46:36.794
Where did this conclusion originate?

46:37.711 --> 46:41.048
Considering the gale
of 100 hectopascals north of the front,

46:41.632 --> 46:44.802
and how fast the North Pacific anticyclone
is expanding,

46:44.885 --> 46:47.221
there was a high chance
that rain clouds would follow.

46:51.725 --> 46:53.352
You think those two
are gonna take a while?

46:53.435 --> 46:55.062
Oh, yeah.

46:59.107 --> 47:02.319
Haven't you heard anything about why
the explanation's going on for so long?

47:02.402 --> 47:04.029
They want to expand it.

47:13.831 --> 47:15.749
Look, I'm right about this.

47:16.500 --> 47:19.878
If you look over here,
this area is too strong for it to rise.

47:19.962 --> 47:21.380
- Hey, Mr. Lee.
- I'm right.

47:21.463 --> 47:23.549
- And it's too warm…
- Listen to me.

47:23.632 --> 47:29.096
The reason this front can move up here
is because of this huge anticyclonic belt.

47:29.179 --> 47:31.139
That's why this can't go down.

47:31.723 --> 47:33.892
You're still missing this whole big one.

47:33.976 --> 47:35.352
Just look at this, will you?

48:14.850 --> 48:16.310
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:16.393 --> 48:17.561
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:24.318 --> 48:25.319
Where is Forecaster Lee?

48:25.402 --> 48:27.195
Oh, he's…

48:27.279 --> 48:29.823
in the Spokesman's Office,
discussing the press release.

48:30.949 --> 48:33.785
I think he said he would send you
an email about your work today.

48:34.536 --> 48:35.662
Ah, here it is. Uh-huh.

48:36.246 --> 48:37.122
Okay.

48:40.208 --> 48:41.835
- Great work.
- You too.

48:41.919 --> 48:43.045
Great work.

48:43.962 --> 48:45.297
Hey, don't worry.

48:45.380 --> 48:47.925
- Door is closing.
- They're not gonna fight again.

48:50.302 --> 48:51.720
Let's all go get some dinner.

48:51.803 --> 48:52.971
- Sure.
- Okay.

48:53.597 --> 48:56.058
- How about something cold?
- Like what?

49:09.821 --> 49:11.740
So it was the wrong call to predict

49:11.823 --> 49:13.825
that the stationary front
would move northward

49:13.909 --> 49:16.578
based on the trough
in central-northern China and the gale.

49:18.664 --> 49:21.875
Anyone would have come
to the same conclusions in the moment.

49:21.959 --> 49:26.129
Mr. Um's theory that the stationary front
would come down was reasonable.

49:26.213 --> 49:28.715
Still, the probability was low.

49:28.799 --> 49:31.385
You always say that you
go off your gut feelings.

49:31.468 --> 49:35.138
But then you blame it all on the data
when your forecast is bad.

49:35.222 --> 49:37.766
To me, that looks like
a pretty lame excuse.

49:39.726 --> 49:41.103
I wasn't sure.

49:43.855 --> 49:45.857
I couldn't risk it on feelings alone.

49:46.733 --> 49:49.194
'Cause too many people's lives
depended on us.

49:49.778 --> 49:50.988
Someone said that to me.

50:03.625 --> 50:06.753
Then tell me why are you going
and risking it all with Ha-kyung?

50:08.130 --> 50:11.091
She looks tough,
but she's a soft soul inside.

50:11.174 --> 50:13.468
The way I already hurt her
was painful enough.

50:13.969 --> 50:15.804
We should focus on the release.

50:15.887 --> 50:17.764
If you're seeing her because you have

50:17.848 --> 50:19.725
some negative feelings
about me or my wife…

50:22.060 --> 50:23.812
Stop, it's not too late.

50:25.605 --> 50:28.025
Ha-kyung doesn't do anything carelessly.

50:28.650 --> 50:32.195
If she really started something with you,
then she's being sincere.

50:32.779 --> 50:34.072
And if she gets hurt again,

50:34.823 --> 50:37.701
there's a chance she won't ever
be able to recover.

50:38.994 --> 50:42.039
Don't you think it's really
not your place to say so

50:42.122 --> 50:43.707
when you're the one that hurt her?

50:43.790 --> 50:45.042
I know that.

50:47.794 --> 50:49.838
I know I seriously hurt her.

50:49.921 --> 50:51.715
That's the reason I'm worried for her.

51:01.058 --> 51:02.601
Don't worry about that, then.

51:03.226 --> 51:07.147
I'm also the type of person
who doesn't start things if I'm not sure.

51:19.159 --> 51:20.994
We can use this as the release.

51:23.872 --> 51:25.248
I'll be going now.

51:29.628 --> 51:31.088
But you should know…

51:38.470 --> 51:40.222
See you next week, Seong-jun.

51:40.305 --> 51:41.515
Okay, good night.

52:55.839 --> 52:56.923
Why…

52:58.466 --> 53:00.343
did you break up with him?

53:02.804 --> 53:03.763
What?

53:03.847 --> 53:06.683
Honestly, even to me,
he seems like a good guy.

53:07.517 --> 53:08.685
No.

53:09.436 --> 53:10.854
Si-woo is a good guy.

53:11.438 --> 53:13.899
Why leave a guy like that
for someone like me?

53:18.111 --> 53:19.571
You really don't know?

53:20.155 --> 53:21.031
No.

53:23.074 --> 53:24.659
I'm asking because I really don't.

53:25.744 --> 53:26.995
You asked me for my hand.

53:30.707 --> 53:32.209
You were the first.

53:33.585 --> 53:36.504
You were the first guy
who wanted to marry me.

53:36.588 --> 53:39.257
Not just go out. You were.

53:43.803 --> 53:45.222
Too bad for you.

53:46.223 --> 53:50.018
The man you married is flat-out broke.

53:53.897 --> 53:55.982
That's why you won't register
our marriage.

54:00.654 --> 54:02.989
Why are you so twisted around?

54:03.073 --> 54:06.993
Do you really think I'd hold up filing
'cause of something like that?

54:07.577 --> 54:08.411
Well, what then?

54:08.495 --> 54:13.208
You never really focused on the issues
between the two of us once we got married.

54:13.959 --> 54:17.587
You were always so focused on what
others would think about all of it.

54:18.171 --> 54:22.050
And now, you're in a crisis because
Jin Ha-kyung might be dating Lee Si-woo

54:22.133 --> 54:24.636
so even now,
you're focused on someone else.

54:25.220 --> 54:28.640
How can I file it if I don't know
if you really love me anymore?

54:30.809 --> 54:31.935
I don't know where we are.

54:32.018 --> 54:34.104
Don't make some excuse about it.

54:35.438 --> 54:36.731
It's all the same thing.

54:37.315 --> 54:40.902
Oppa, stop running around all the time!
If you love me, focus!

55:13.852 --> 55:15.895
Oh.

55:16.688 --> 55:18.398
Did you and Ki-jun have a run-in again?

55:21.067 --> 55:22.360
I want to do better.

55:22.444 --> 55:24.029
- What?
- Huh?

55:24.696 --> 55:26.156
The stationary front.

55:27.032 --> 55:29.576
- Let's analyze it again.
- Why?

55:29.659 --> 55:31.870
Is there an unusual signal or something?

55:31.953 --> 55:35.123
No, I discovered this when I was working
on the report with Director Han earlier.

55:35.206 --> 55:36.249
Here.

55:37.417 --> 55:40.086
The Okhotsk Sea air mass
that was abnormally developing

55:40.170 --> 55:41.713
isn't expanding anymore.

55:41.796 --> 55:43.840
And there's vapor coming in
from the southwest.

55:43.923 --> 55:47.802
Isn't it still too weak for
the North Pacific anticyclone to start?

55:47.886 --> 55:49.804
- What do you think?
- I agree with you.

55:50.430 --> 55:53.016
Uh, look at this part over here.

55:53.099 --> 55:55.977
The rain particles get stronger
as it rises, don't they?

55:56.561 --> 55:58.438
Hmm. I'm not so sure.

55:58.521 --> 56:01.191
If the anticyclone on the Okhotsk Sea
stops developing

56:01.274 --> 56:02.901
and vapor keeps coming in
from the southwest,

56:02.984 --> 56:05.320
the North Pacific anticyclone will expand.

56:05.403 --> 56:09.366
And if all that's true,
I'd say it's two days till rain.

56:21.920 --> 56:24.422
Let's go with Mr. Lee's thoughts
this time.

56:24.506 --> 56:27.050
It's true that the southwest
shows a lot of vapor right now.

56:28.051 --> 56:30.512
Well, okay, then. Okay.

56:30.595 --> 56:33.556
Thank you for, uh, believing me.

56:39.270 --> 56:42.065
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

57:07.340 --> 57:11.428
THE KMA'S WEATHER FORECAST
IS WRONG AGAIN

57:19.227 --> 57:21.604
THE FORECAST IS WRONG AGAIN
WHAT IS THE PROBLEM?

57:33.366 --> 57:35.702
The KMA's forecast was wrong yet again.

57:35.785 --> 57:37.120
Why do you think that is?

57:37.620 --> 57:41.916
Global warming's speeding up,
and we see this with El Niño and La Niña.

57:42.000 --> 57:44.627
And the variables of forecasting
grow more complicated.

57:44.711 --> 57:46.546
Could you please put that
in simpler terms?

57:47.547 --> 57:50.758
In short, the climate is a car
ignoring all traffic lights

57:50.842 --> 57:52.969
and we're trying to guess
which way it's going to go.

57:55.889 --> 57:57.599
The reporters are loving this.

57:57.682 --> 58:01.686
Also, because no big stuff's happened
for a while.

58:01.769 --> 58:03.062
Poor Ms. Jin.

58:03.146 --> 58:05.773
She's been suffering
ever since they made her director.

58:06.816 --> 58:09.068
Nothing's working out for her.

58:25.960 --> 58:27.337
Aren't you tired?

58:30.924 --> 58:31.925
Let's go in now.

58:34.344 --> 58:35.470
I'm sorry.

58:35.553 --> 58:37.430
I shouldn't have insisted.

58:39.474 --> 58:40.892
We wouldn't have gotten it wrong.

58:42.685 --> 58:44.437
You didn't get it wrong.

58:45.146 --> 58:47.357
And it's not like
Mr. Um and I were right either.

58:49.484 --> 58:52.195
You said it yourself.
Weather is a variability.

58:52.779 --> 58:56.658
One tiny factor sometimes gets
to change the whole scene.

58:57.617 --> 58:58.785
What are we gonna do?

59:01.371 --> 59:03.498
Take our licks as we were wrong.

59:28.439 --> 59:29.691
THE KMA'S ERRONEOUS FORECAST

59:29.774 --> 59:34.654
The KMA has forecast a rainfall
of 50 to 100mm an hour in Seoul, Gyeonggi,

59:34.737 --> 59:37.365
Yeongseo and Gangwon,
starting early this morning.

59:38.032 --> 59:41.578
But currently, most areas
are only cloudy with no rain.

59:41.661 --> 59:44.372
Although we did avoid
a rainy morning commute today,

59:44.455 --> 59:46.583
many are complaining that they are tired…

59:46.666 --> 59:49.669
Bo-mi, I have a bit
of a headache right now.

59:49.752 --> 59:51.004
- Can you…
- Okay.

59:51.629 --> 59:53.339
- The KMA's forecast was wrong yet again.
- Wait.

59:53.423 --> 59:54.966
Why do you think that is?

59:57.176 --> 01:00:01.598
Global warming's speeding up,
and we see this with El Niño and La Niña.

01:00:01.681 --> 01:00:04.225
And the variables of forecasting
grow more complicated.

01:00:05.518 --> 01:00:09.022
In short, the climate
is a car ignoring all traffic lights

01:00:09.105 --> 01:00:11.357
and we're trying to guess
which way it's going to go.

01:00:11.441 --> 01:00:13.651
- That sounds like a very difficult task.
- You know that woman?

01:00:13.735 --> 01:00:15.361
- Yeah.
- Shouldn't your supercomputers

01:00:15.445 --> 01:00:17.405
with their vast amount of accumulated data

01:00:17.488 --> 01:00:19.824
be able to account
for all those variables?

01:00:24.078 --> 01:00:24.954
Thank you.

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.343
You said weather's harder to predict

01:00:38.426 --> 01:00:40.970
'cause climate change
has increased so rapidly of late.

01:00:41.721 --> 01:00:43.681
Shouldn't something be done about that?

01:00:44.474 --> 01:00:49.896
Well, that's the reason we have the NWP,
so we can have more predictive power.

01:00:49.979 --> 01:00:53.107
So there's no clear fix for it?

01:00:54.108 --> 01:00:55.735
Well, we'll try our very best.

01:00:58.154 --> 01:00:59.405
Trying is easy.

01:01:00.615 --> 01:01:02.909
What's hard is doing your job well.

01:01:03.951 --> 01:01:04.869
Is this over?

01:01:05.995 --> 01:01:07.955
- Yes.
- Well, thank you.

01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:12.001
I heard that you're dating Si-woo.

01:01:16.005 --> 01:01:18.758
Did Han Ki-jun say that?
I told him it's not the truth.

01:01:19.676 --> 01:01:21.844
Well, he is charming.

01:01:23.179 --> 01:01:24.972
Innocent but intelligent.

01:01:25.932 --> 01:01:29.435
He's penniless, but at least
he has some self-confidence.

01:01:30.687 --> 01:01:32.689
And he's not hard on the eyes either.

01:01:36.109 --> 01:01:37.735
Can I ask you a question?

01:01:40.029 --> 01:01:42.156
Why break up with such
a good man like Si-woo?

01:01:43.282 --> 01:01:46.327
Is it because of his father?

01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:53.835
You think you know everything, huh?

01:01:56.170 --> 01:02:00.425
Si-woo's father, I know he's sleazy.

01:02:01.592 --> 01:02:04.846
But not so bad
that I would break up with him for it.

01:02:06.597 --> 01:02:07.849
Then why…

01:02:10.017 --> 01:02:11.310
Si-woo oppa…

01:02:12.603 --> 01:02:13.813
doesn't want marriage.

01:02:16.357 --> 01:02:20.403
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

01:02:33.040 --> 01:02:34.208
Oh, you should know.

01:02:34.292 --> 01:02:38.921
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody
unless there's a chance of marriage.

01:02:40.339 --> 01:02:42.258
You are aware of that, right?

01:02:50.141 --> 01:02:52.852
Door is opening.

01:02:53.686 --> 01:02:54.812
Going up.

01:02:58.816 --> 01:03:00.318
Uh, wait for me.

01:03:00.401 --> 01:03:01.652
Oh!

01:03:02.361 --> 01:03:03.446
Hello.

01:03:12.580 --> 01:03:15.041
The same way
flowers bloom in spring

01:03:15.124 --> 01:03:18.044
and the rainy season comes in summer,

01:03:18.669 --> 01:03:22.673
marriage always felt
like a natural progression for me.

01:03:24.842 --> 01:03:26.511
However, with climate change

01:03:26.594 --> 01:03:30.181
and the growing uncertainty
of weather forecasting nowadays…

01:03:30.264 --> 01:03:31.682
Si-woo oppa…

01:03:32.850 --> 01:03:34.143
doesn't want marriage.

01:03:36.687 --> 01:03:40.650
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

01:03:40.733 --> 01:03:44.570
What really is natural
to us anymore?

01:04:25.486 --> 01:04:27.780
I hadn't considered it
really till now,

01:04:27.864 --> 01:04:30.157
not getting married after dating.

01:04:30.241 --> 01:04:32.743
Who are you? My daughter lives here.

01:04:32.827 --> 01:04:34.036
- Oh?
- Uh…

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:36.163
All of you are living together
because of your work?

01:04:36.247 --> 01:04:38.916
In the elevator,
there was a man you were talking to.

01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:40.877
How exactly does he know you?

01:04:41.502 --> 01:04:42.545
Thanks.

01:04:42.628 --> 01:04:43.671
Are you an only child?

01:04:43.754 --> 01:04:44.714
Why are you asking me?

01:04:44.797 --> 01:04:45.882
What's with the temperature in Yeouido?

01:04:45.965 --> 01:04:48.968
Take it down now and put a blink up
on the weather portal.

01:04:49.051 --> 01:04:51.345
The error on the disaster
prevention portal,

01:04:51.429 --> 01:04:53.014
you tipped him off, didn't you?

01:04:53.723 --> 01:04:55.516
You should have submitted
a report to me right away!
